# Tampa Volunteers Platform

## Project Overview
Tampa Volunteers is a volunteer management platform connecting community members with local volunteer opportunities in the Tampa Bay area. Organizations post volunteer needs and individuals discover and sign up for opportunities matching their interests.

## Architecture
- **Backend**: Spring Boot (Java) - REST API
- **Frontend**: Vite (React/Vue) - SPA
- **Database**: PostgreSQL
- **Structure**: Monorepo or separate repos (tampavolunteers-backend, tampavolunteers-frontend)

## Tech Stack

### Backend
- Spring Boot 3.x
- Spring Security + JWT authentication
- Spring Data JPA / Hibernate
- PostgreSQL JDBC driver
- Flyway/Liquibase for migrations
- Swagger/OpenAPI for documentation
- Maven build tool

### Frontend
- Vite dev server
- React/Vue framework
- React Router/Vue Router
- Axios for API calls
- TailwindCSS or Material-UI
- Environment-based configuration

## Repository Structure

### Backend (tampavolunteers-backend/)
```
src/main/java/org/tampavolunteers/
  ├── controller/          # REST endpoints
  ├── service/             # Business logic
  ├── repository/          # JPA repositories
  ├── model/               # Entity classes
  ├── dto/                 # Data transfer objects
  ├── config/              # Spring configuration
  ├── security/            # Auth & authorization
  └── exception/           # Custom exceptions

src/main/resources/
  ├── application.properties
  ├── application-dev.properties
  ├── application-prod.properties
  └── db/migration/        # Database migrations

pom.xml
```

### Frontend (tampavolunteers-frontend/)
```
src/
  ├── components/          # Reusable UI components
  ├── pages/               # Page components
  ├── services/            # API service layer
  ├── hooks/               # Custom React hooks
  ├── context/             # React Context/Store
  ├── utils/               # Helper functions
  ├── types/               # TypeScript types
  └── assets/              # Images, fonts, etc.

public/
package.json
vite.config.js
.env.development
.env.production
```

## Data Model

### Core Entities

**User**
- id (UUID/Long)
- email (unique)
- passwordHash
- firstName, lastName
- phone
- role (VOLUNTEER, ORG_ADMIN, ADMIN)
- createdAt, updatedAt

**Organization**
- id
- name
- description
- website
- contactEmail, contactPhone
- address (street, city, state, zip)
- verified (boolean)
- userId (admin user)
- createdAt

**Opportunity**
- id
- organizationId
- title
- description
- startDateTime, endDateTime
- location (address fields)
- slotsAvailable, slotsFilled
- categoryId
- skillsRequired (many-to-many)
- status (DRAFT, PUBLISHED, CANCELLED, COMPLETED)
- createdAt, updatedAt

**Registration**
- id
- opportunityId
- userId
- status (PENDING, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED, COMPLETED)
- registeredAt
- attendanceConfirmed (boolean)

**VolunteerHours**
- id
- registrationId
- userId
- opportunityId
- hoursLogged (decimal)
- verifiedBy (userId)
- notes
- loggedAt

**Category**
- id
- name (Environment, Education, Health, Animals, etc.)
- description

**Skill**
- id
- name (Teaching, Construction, Medical, etc.)

## API Endpoints

### Authentication
- POST /api/auth/register - Register new user
- POST /api/auth/login - Login and get JWT
- POST /api/auth/refresh - Refresh JWT token
- POST /api/auth/logout - Logout
- GET /api/auth/me - Get current user

### Opportunities
- GET /api/opportunities - List/search opportunities (public)
- GET /api/opportunities/{id} - Get opportunity details
- POST /api/opportunities - Create (ORG_ADMIN)
- PUT /api/opportunities/{id} - Update (ORG_ADMIN)
- DELETE /api/opportunities/{id} - Delete (ORG_ADMIN)
- GET /api/opportunities/search - Advanced search with filters

### Registrations
- POST /api/registrations - Volunteer registers for opportunity
- GET /api/registrations/user/{userId} - User's registrations
- GET /api/registrations/opportunity/{id} - Registrations for opportunity
- PUT /api/registrations/{id}/status - Update registration status
- DELETE /api/registrations/{id} - Cancel registration

### Organizations
- GET /api/organizations - List organizations
- GET /api/organizations/{id} - Get organization details
- POST /api/organizations - Create organization
- PUT /api/organizations/{id} - Update organization
- GET /api/organizations/{id}/opportunities - Org's opportunities

### Volunteer Hours
- POST /api/volunteer-hours - Log hours
- GET /api/volunteer-hours/user/{userId} - User's logged hours
- PUT /api/volunteer-hours/{id}/verify - Verify hours (ORG_ADMIN)
- GET /api/volunteer-hours/report - Generate report

### Categories & Skills
- GET /api/categories - List all categories
- GET /api/skills - List all skills

## Configuration

### Backend (application.properties)
```properties
# Database
spring.datasource.url=jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/tampavolunteers
spring.datasource.username=${DB_USERNAME}
spring.datasource.password=${DB_PASSWORD}
spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=validate
spring.jpa.properties.hibernate.dialect=org.hibernate.dialect.PostgreSQLDialect

# Server
server.port=8080
server.servlet.context-path=/api

# JWT
jwt.secret=${JWT_SECRET}
jwt.expiration=86400000

# CORS
cors.allowed-origins=http://localhost:5173

# Email (optional)
spring.mail.host=${MAIL_HOST}
spring.mail.port=587
```

### Frontend (.env)
```env
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080/api
VITE_APP_NAME=Tampa Volunteers
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=${GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY}
```

