```

## Security Implementation

### Authentication Flow
1. User submits credentials to /api/auth/login
2. Backend validates and returns JWT token
3. Frontend stores token (localStorage)
4. Frontend includes token in Authorization header: `Bearer {token}`
5. Backend validates token on protected endpoints

### Authorization
- VOLUNTEER: Can browse opportunities, register, log hours
- ORG_ADMIN: All volunteer permissions + manage own organization & opportunities
- ADMIN: Full platform access, approve organizations

### Password Security
- BCrypt hashing (strength 12)
- Minimum 8 characters required
- No plain text storage

## Database Indexes
- users.email (unique)
- opportunities.organizationId
- opportunities.startDateTime
- opportunities.categoryId
- registrations.userId
- registrations.opportunityId
- volunteer_hours.userId

## Frontend Key Features

### Pages
- / - Landing page with search
- /opportunities - Browse opportunities
- /opportunities/{id} - Opportunity details
- /login, /register - Authentication
- /dashboard - User dashboard
- /dashboard/volunteer - Volunteer's registrations & hours
- /dashboard/organization - Org admin management
- /profile - User profile settings

### State Management
- User authentication state
- Current user profile
- Opportunity filters
- Registration status

## Error Handling

### Backend
- Global exception handler with @ControllerAdvice
- Standard error response format:
```json
{
  "timestamp": "2025-10-17T10:30:00",
  "status": 400,
  "error": "Bad Request",
  "message": "Invalid email format",
  "path": "/api/auth/register"
}
```

### Frontend
- Toast notifications for user feedback
- Error boundary components
- API error interceptors
- Form validation with clear messages

## Testing Strategy

### Backend Tests
- Unit tests: Service layer logic
- Integration tests: Repository & database
- API tests: Controller endpoints with MockMvc
- Test database: H2 or Testcontainers PostgreSQL

### Frontend Tests
- Unit tests: Component logic
- Integration tests: User flows
- E2E tests: Critical paths (Playwright/Cypress)

## Deployment

### Backend
- Build: `./mvnw clean package`
- Docker image with embedded Tomcat
- Environment variables for secrets
- Health check endpoint: /api/actuator/health

### Frontend
- Build: `npm run build` → dist/
- Deploy static files to CDN/hosting
- Environment variables injected at build time
- Reverse proxy for API (/api → backend)

### Database
- Managed PostgreSQL instance (AWS RDS, etc.)
- Automated backups
- Connection pooling (HikariCP)
- SSL/TLS connections in production

## Code Style

### Backend (Java)
- Google Java Style Guide
- Lombok for boilerplate reduction
- Constructor injection for dependencies
- RESTful naming conventions
- Comprehensive Javadoc for public APIs

### Frontend
- ESLint + Prettier
- Functional components with hooks
- Named exports for components
- Absolute imports with path aliases (@/)
- PropTypes or TypeScript for type safety

